Binaryen 131's --spill-pointers for collecting only at interrupt checks, with ruby-4.0-jspi-safepoint-gc.patch, an
experiment, from binaryen-131-spill-pointers.patch: a call's spilled around only if what it calls can reach the
function spill-pointers-gc names and return, or it's in a try, which catches a jump, and can reach it at all, as a
frame a jump unwinds through never resumes. An indirect call reaches it through the functions of its type in a table,
and calls to the functions spill-pointers-cut names don't. Applied to Binaryen's source, and built, as that patch
says, then run in place of the configure's --spill-pointers as
  --flatten --coalesce-locals --spill-pointers --pass-arg=spill-pointers-gc@rb_wasm_safepoint_gc \
    --pass-arg=spill-pointers-cut@garbage_collect,gc_start,gc_rest,gc_continue -O3
with SPILL_POINTERS_DEBUG set to say how many functions can collect, and SPILL_POINTERS_WHY, functions separated by
commas, for how each can.

